# American English: only the lines that differ from English. The rest is English.

settings-network-join-password-kept = The saved password for this network wasn't accepted. Use the trash can button to forget the network, then join it again.

settings-network-in-range-about = Every Wi-Fi network this computer can pick up. When you open the page, the network you are using comes first, then saved networks, then the rest by signal strength. The order doesn't change while the page is open. Press the arrow to join a network. A secured network asks for its password the first time. The trash can button forgets a saved network and its password. An open network isn't encrypted, so people nearby could see what you send over it.

settings-network-kept-anyway = { $words } The network was saved anyway. Forget it with the trash can button before joining again.
